-- title:
--   The predual of a Hopf order of the Cartier dual
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative domain which is a principal ideal ring, with field of fractions $K$ (so $R$ is an $R$-subalgebra of $K$ and $K$ is its fraction field), and let $A$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $K$ which is finite-dimensional as a $K$-module and whose comultiplication is cocommutative, together with an $R$-algebra structure compatible with the $K$-structure; the $K$-linear dual $\mathrm{CartierDual}\,K\,A = \mathrm{Module.Dual}\,K\,A$, with its Hopf algebra structure over $K$, is likewise assumed to carry a compatible $R$-algebra structure. Let $T$ be an $R$-subalgebra of this dual which is (i) finite as an $R$-module, (ii) $K$-spanning, in the sense that the $K$-submodule generated by $T$ is all of the dual, (iii) stable under comultiplication in the weak sense that for every $x \in T$ the element $\mathrm{comul}(x)$ of $(\mathrm{CartierDual}\,K\,A) \otimes_K (\mathrm{CartierDual}\,K\,A)$ lies in the range of the $R$-algebra map out of $T \otimes_R T$ obtained by multiplying the two inclusions $t \mapsto t \otimes 1$ and $t \mapsto 1 \otimes t$, (iv) stable under the antipode, and (v) such that the counit of every $x \in T$ lies in the image of $R$ in $K$. Then there exists an $R$-subalgebra $S$ of $A$ with the property that an element $a \in A$ belongs to $S$ precisely when $\varphi(a)$ lies in the image of $R$ in $K$ for every $\varphi \in T$, and such that $S$ satisfies the same five conditions relative to $A$: $S$ is finite as an $R$-module, its $K$-span is all of $A$, for every $x \in S$ the element $\mathrm{comul}(x)$ of $A \otimes_K A$ lies in the range of the $R$-algebra map from $S \otimes_R S$ built from the two inclusions of $S$ into $A \otimes_K A$, $S$ is stable under the antipode of $A$, and the counit of every element of $S$ lies in the image of $R$ in $K$.
--
--   This is one half of the duality between Hopf orders in a finite cocommutative Hopf algebra $A$ over $K$ and Hopf orders in its Cartier dual: the predual lattice $\{a \in A : \varphi(a) \in R \text{ for all } \varphi \in T\}$ of a Hopf order $T$ of the dual is again a Hopf order, the statement being formulated directly in $A$ without passing through the double dual. It is used in the construction of the least Hopf order of $A$, [`HopfOrder.exists_isLeast`](thm.html#HopfOrder.exists_isLeast), which is obtained as the predual of the greatest Hopf order of the Cartier dual.
